om/sveltejs/kit.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/sveltejs/kit","homepage":"https://svelte.dev/docs/kit","size":32161,"stargazers_count":20055,"watchers_count":20055,"language":"JavaScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":2168,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":1040,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["hacktoberfest","svelte"],"visibility":"public","forks":2168,"open_issues":1040,"watchers":20055,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"To catch a 404 Error I created a Falltrough Route, since $error isnt called (at least in dev). This is needed, because 404 leads to a infinete reload till a route is created. But it failed to subfolders. Falltrough Routes does not affect subdirs.\r\n\r\nroutes/[404].svelte\r\nworks for all routes in root dir. When I call a subfolder like http://localhost:3000/Town/Shop I have to create  a routes/Town/[404.svelte] as well.\r\n\r\nNow I'm at a point asking me some questions?\r\n\r\nShould fallthrough Routes be catched by parent folders as well?\r\nHow can I catch the 404 Error and handle it by my own code?\r\n\r\nMaybe we should be able to create a custom error 404 page, like $e404.svelte (similiar to $error.svelte)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sveltejs/kit/issues/1255/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sveltejs/kit/issues/1255/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]